# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# K-Beauty Bliss — far-future caching for content-addressed files
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT SHIPPED BY A PACKAGE AND IS NOT APPLIED AUTOMATICALLY.
# docs/ is on BuildPackage::NEVER_SHIP, so nothing here can reach the server by
# accident. Read docs/IMAGE-PIPELINE-AND-CACHE.md §9 before installing it by
# hand; it says where it goes, how to check the web root first, and what to do
# if the assets stop loading afterwards.
#
# It contains NO RewriteRule, NO Options and nothing outside an <IfModule>
# guard. That is deliberate: this file must not be able to change how a single
# URL is routed. On a server with mod_headers it sets the policy below; on one
# without, every directive inside the guard is skipped and the file does
# nothing at all.
#
# WHY A YEAR IS SAFE HERE AND NOWHERE ELSE ON THIS SITE
#
#   /build/     Vite writes content-hashed names — kbb-NawQuIF5.css — and a
#               rebuild produces a new name. A URL under here cannot ever
#               answer with different bytes.
#   /img-cache/ the generated phone-sized copies. Their names mirror originals
#               named Ymd-His-<random>.ext, and MediaUploadController cannot
#               overwrite an original, so a variant URL is as fixed as the
#               photograph it was made from.
#
# Neither property is assumed: tests/Feature/CacheHeaderPolicyTest.php asserts
# both, and holds the max-age below to App\Http\Middleware\CacheHeaders::IMMUTABLE
# so this file and the application cannot state different numbers.
#
# HTML IS NOT CACHED HERE. It is the application's to decide and it decides it
# in that middleware: a storefront page carries a cart badge and a CSRF token
# and must never be held by a shared cache.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

<IfModule mod_headers.c>
    <FilesMatch "\.(css|js|mjs|map|jpe?g|png|webp|gif|svg|ico|woff2?)$">
        Header set Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable"
    </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
